pcbnew: construct point-on-line candidates in place

computeAnchors built a NEARABLE_GEOM from the visited alternative and
then copied that variant into the candidate vector. Every
INTERSECTABLE_GEOM alternative is also a NEARABLE_GEOM alternative, so
emplacing the alternative directly builds the same variant and drops the
copy.

It also drops a -Wmaybe-uninitialized false positive: GCC cannot track
which alternative is engaged across the intermediate variant's
copy-construction, so it reported the BOX2I alternative's storage as
possibly-uninitialised.

diff --git a/pcbnew/tools/pcb_grid_helper.cpp b/pcbnew/tools/pcb_grid_helper.cpp
index bc6366db34..8a53800c02 100644
--- a/pcbnew/tools/pcb_grid_helper.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/tools/pcb_grid_helper.cpp
@@ -1255,8 +1255,7 @@ void PCB_GRID_HELPER::computeAnchors( const std::vector<BOARD_ITEM*>& aItems,
             std::visit(
                     [&]( const auto& geom )
                     {
-                        NEARABLE_GEOM nearable( geom );
-                        m_pointOnLineCandidates.emplace_back( nearable );
+                        m_pointOnLineCandidates.emplace_back( geom );
                     },
                     intersectable.Geometry );
         }
